eli: hitting a weird thing on emulator with okhttp + our Android SDK. Requests to /v1/chat sometimes hang for 20-30s then fail. Only on emulator and only when backgrounding app. Anyone seen this?

sara: hmm, sounds like dispatcher starvation or retry loop. which okhttp/client config? setRetryOnConnectionFailure?

eli: using default client from SDK: OkHttpClient.Builder().addInterceptor(AuthInterceptor).build() — didn't touch retry flag. Also we do token refresh in an interceptor when 401. emulator logs show "response code: 401" then repeated clones until timeout.

michael: classic double-refresh. Authenticator should handle 401-level refresh, interceptors add header. If both try to refresh you get races and queue up requests. Also emulator network can pause sockets when app backgrounded.

ana: can you paste interceptor/Authenticator snippets? Also try setting dispatcher.maxRequestsPerHost small? or call.timeout?

eli: pasted snippet: ```kotlin
class AuthInterceptor: Interceptor {
  override fun intercept(chain: Interceptor.Chain): Response {
    val token = tokenProvider.getToken() // may refresh
    return chain.proceed(chain.request().newBuilder().header("Authorization", "Bearer $token").build())
  }
}

class TokenAuthenticator: Authenticator {
  override fun authenticate(route: Route?, response: Response): Request? {
    val newToken = tokenProvider.refreshToken()
    return response.request.newBuilder().header("Authorization", "Bearer $newToken").build()
  }
}
```

sara: There's the problem: tokenProvider.refreshToken() might be synchronized poorly and called from multiple threads. On 401 OkHttp will call Authenticator concurrently for queued calls. Use a single-refresh Mutex or use refresh flow that returns same deferred for inflight refreshes.

michael: quick fix: make tokenProvider.refreshToken() check cached ongoing refresh: ```kotlin
@Volatile private var ongoing: Deferred<String>? = null
suspend fun refreshTokenSuspend(): String = coroutineScope {
  ongoing?.let { return it.await() }
  val d = async { networkRefresh() }
  ongoing = d
  try { return d.await() } finally { ongoing = null }
}
```

ana: also try client.newBuilder().authenticator(TokenAuthenticator()).retryOnConnectionFailure(false).callTimeout(30, TimeUnit.SECONDS).build() — reduces duplicate tries and helps emulator weirdness.

deploy-bot: sdk-release-0.13.2 deployed to canary containing android okhttp fixes :rocket:

eli: thanks — I'll try replacing refresh-in-interceptor with header-only interceptor + Authenticator + shared refresh promise. Will test on emulator and real devices and report back.

sara: if it still flakes, try enabling okhttp event listener for slow calls to capture socket pauses: `OkHttpClient.eventListenerFactory(MyListener.Factory())`.

eli: will do, thx :thumbsup:
